{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgthBFmUXz8Cqw1PFQbSy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The surviving failures are a different kind of loop. In the original model, 91% of loop units contained a doubt word. Under the brake only 10.6% do, yet 254 of 512 samples still loop, with a similar period (about 44 tokens) and onset (median 7.3k tokens). In 73% of GSM8K cases the right answer was already written before the loop started. The new loops are bullet-list restatements: the model re-lists the same facts (\"* x-y = 3\", \"* x+y = -1\", \"* E is midpoint of AD\", ...), often at deep indentation. So the brake removed the doubt-driven cycle, but the underlying copy-and-continue dynamics now find another cycle: non-doubt loops went from about 41 samples to about 227. A stronger brake is therefore unlikely to be the main next lever, and the next target is how restatement loops start. I will read the text just before several loop onsets and measure the indentation depth inside these loops against pre-loop text, to see whether the onset is a recognizable decision (for example an end-of-list point where the model restarts the list instead of concluding).\n\n```python\n# Hypothesis: x2 surviving loops start at end-of-list decision points (model restarts a bullet list instead of concluding), often deeply nested.\ndef squeeze(s): return re.sub(r' {3,}', lambda m: f'<{len(m.group())}sp>', s)\nnd = LU11[~LU11.doubt]\nfor _, r in nd.sample(5, random_state=1).iterrows():\n    rec = next(x for x in g11r if x['id'] == r['id']); s = rec['samples'][int(r['si'])]\n    enc_ = tok.encode(s['text']); cpos = enc_.offsets[r['onset']][0]\n    print(f\"--- {r['id']} si{r['si']} period {r['period']} onset {r['onset']}\")\n    print('PRE :', asc_(squeeze(s['text'][max(0, cpos-260):cpos])).replace('\\n', ' / '))\n    print('LOOP:', asc_(squeeze(s['text'][cpos:cpos+160])).replace('\\n', ' / '))\ndef max_indent(t): return max([len(l) - len(l.lstrip(' ')) for l in t.split('\\n') if l.strip()] + [0])\nprint('median max-indent in loop unit: x2 nondoubt', np.median([max_indent(u) for u in nd.unit]), '| orig doubt units', np.median([max_indent(u) for u in LU2[LU2.doubt].unit]))\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1917,"cache_read_input_tokens":34045,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1917},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b4bcd242-3053-49df-a015-76e7a59477b0","uuid":"2a82e555-9d09-47de-9804-e8f25feb18fb","timestamp":"2026-11-10T05:27:55.375Z","request_id":"req_011CgthBFb56NUvFZJjRJiq5"}
